  "body": "Fork synced at v0.17.0. Effort: high (no escalation).\n\n## Root causes (#866)\n\n1. **The carry refusal is correct by design, not a frame bug.** The viewport draws the active setup's frame, so the plate standing upright in Setup2 means the plate is modelled lying flat and Setup2 holds it turned X -90° (a part-alignment change on Setup2; `CreateSetup` itself never sets one - with \"Carry stock and WCS over\" it copies Setup1's). Setup1 holds it as modelled, so the turn *between* the setups is a real side-on quarter turn about X, which the column lattice of the carried stock cannot re-index (`CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL`). `setup_relative::transform_between` already composes `A_to * A_from^-1` (the relative turn): two setups holding the part alike - both turned X -90° - carry fine, now pinned. The unpicked stock source of a setup that holds the part differently defaults to the carry (#317's rule), which is why the refused option shows selected but disabled. Lifting the limit is filed as **#874** (effort:max, after the field engine #637 / #586).\n2. **The \"35 s freeze\" was the user's time in the file dialog.** The native dialogs (rfd) are modal and synchronous and open from `State::drain_actions`, inside the frame's \"commands\" phase; the frame watch (#74) counted the browsing time as app work. The log's xdg-desktop-portal warning (the dialog opening) sits right before the slow frame; the STEP tessellates off-thread as before. (**#872**)\n3. **Jargon** - \"furniture\" is our in-code word for a setup's stock, WCS and fixtures; the refusal text named neither the turn nor a way out. (**#873**)\n\n## What changed\n- `crates/app/src/stock_sim_carry.rs`: a turn refusal names the relative turn, \"'Setup2' holds the part turned X -90°, Y 0°, Z 0° from how 'Setup1' holds it, and <CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL>\".\n- `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/carry.rs`: `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL` kept by name, reworded: \"the stock simulation can carry machined stock only through a flip over X or Y or a quarter turn about Z (turns that keep the tool axis vertical) - any other turn would have to re-sample the stock and lose its detail\".\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_stock_pick.rs`: the page says what happened and what to do - choose \"Its own stock\", or hold the part as the previous setup does (a flip over X/Y or a turn about Z also works).\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/setup_pages.rs`, `pages.rs`: the radio reads \"Active setup - new operations go into it, and the Stock and Work offset pages edit it\"; the Setups page footer drops \"furniture\".\n- `crates/ui/src/file_dialog.rs`, `frame_watch.rs`, `shell_window/frame.rs`: every modal dialog is timed (`file_dialog::take_waited`) and the frame watch takes that time off the frame (`FrameWatch::excuse`); work beyond the wait is still reported.\n- `docs/decisions/866-setup2-carry.md`.\n\n## How tested\nPinning tests (all pass locally on macOS, clippy `-D warnings` clean on sim/app/ui):\n- `setup_stock_source::both_setups_turned_alike_carry_through_the_identity` - the relative-turn composition.\n- `setup_stock_source::a_side_on_turn_between_setups_is_refused_naming_the_turn` - the refusal names the turn and keeps `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL`.\n- `egui_app::frame_watch::tests::time_in_a_modal_dialog_is_not_a_slow_frame`.\n- `egui_app::setup_stock_tests::the_settings_page_has_no_in_code_jargon`; `a_refused_carry_disables_the_option_with_its_reason` extended with the turn and the way out.\n- Re-ran `setup_carry`, `carried_verify`, `camcraft-sim stock_carry` (they match on `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL`): green.\n- Linux quick gate: see the comment below.\n\n## Not exercised\n- The reporter's own STEP file (not attached); reproduced with a flat plate mesh turned X -90° in Setup2.\n- A live run of a native file dialog (the timing seam is pinned at the frame-watch level; the dialog itself is not driven in tests).\n- Snapshot PNGs untouched (release lane).\n\nChangelog: The setup page names the turn that stops the stock carry and says what to do, drops the \"furniture\" jargon, and the slow-frame log no longer blames time spent in a file dialog (#866, #872, #873)\n\nFixes #872\nFixes #873\nRefs #866\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
